    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **285 tests, 0 failures**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the requirement that owner creation is rejected with **400 Bad Request** when the owner's city already contains 8 owners.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n- Added a city-capacity check after the existing daily-limit check. The check runs *after* `resolveCity(...)`, so it uses the canonicalized city and matches existing owners case-insensitively (consistent with the existing `nextCustomerCode` city matching).\n- Added a private `isCityCapacityReached(String city)` helper that counts existing owners in the city and returns `true` when the count is \u2265 8. A `null` city is treated as not-full.\n\n**Tests** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`:\n- `createOwnerRejectedWhenCityFull` \u2014 8 owners already in the city (verifying case-insensitive matching via a differently-cased city in the request) \u2192 expects 400.\n- `createOwnerAllowedWhenCityBelowCapacity` \u2014 7 owners in the city \u2192 expects 201 Created.\n\nBoth new tests follow the existing daily-limit test conventions.",
